WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:23.270
"Wow!" Perda exclaimed. "First City is huge!"

2
00:00:23.271 --> 00:00:27.919
Zann hadn't been back to the capital since he and Boz had moved to Swamp Bottom.

3
00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.715
He leaned forward, searching for a glimpse of his old neighborhood.

4
00:00:31.716 --> 00:00:39.070
But it was hard to get his bearings from way up in the sky, and before he knew it, the dragons were circling lower and lower.

5
00:00:39.071 --> 00:00:41.985
They landed in a clearing outside of town.

6
00:00:41.986 --> 00:00:45.837
"This looks like a safe spot for the dragons to rest," Darb said.

7
00:00:45.838 --> 00:00:48.889
Zann's legs felt stiff as he jumped down.

8
00:00:48.890 --> 00:00:54.482
The dragons had flown swiftly, but it had taken almost two hours to reach their destination.

9
00:00:54.483 --> 00:00:59.586
"Now what?" Gliss asked. "Does anyone know how to get to the palace?"

10
00:00:59.587 --> 00:01:04.654
Zann reached into his pocket, checking to make sure Boz's diary was still there.

11
00:01:04.655 --> 00:01:10.287
"I remember my way around well enough," he said. "I'll find it."

12
00:01:10.288 --> 00:01:17.573
They hiked through the woods. As soon as Zann saw the ramshackle buildings at the city limits, he realized where they were.

13
00:01:17.574 --> 00:01:24.348
"This area is called Wormwood," he told the others. "It's not the best part of town."

14
00:01:24.349 --> 00:01:28.632
"Really?" Gliss said nervously. "What's wrong with it?"

15
00:01:28.633 --> 00:01:35.886
"Everyone says it got its name because there's a wormhole near some gnarled old tree here," Zann explained.

16
00:01:35.887 --> 00:01:40.908
"And that the locals figured out how to use it to bring stuff back from other worlds."

17
00:01:40.909 --> 00:01:49.554
"I've read about that," Darb said. "People say there's a thriving black market here for exotic otherworld pets and stuff."

18
00:01:49.555 --> 00:01:53.919
"Sounds cool, but let's remember why we're here, okay?" said Perda.

19
00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:58.421
"We need to get that diary to the palace."

20
00:01:58.422 --> 00:02:04.721
Zann knew she was right. Still, he couldn't help watching for the notorious tree as he walked.

21
00:02:04.722 --> 00:02:07.274
"Is that it?" Darb pointed.

22
00:02:07.275 --> 00:02:13.527
Just ahead was a tree so ancient and twisted that it appeared to be carved out of stone.

23
00:02:13.528 --> 00:02:19.536
Several huts stood near its massive trunk, their entrances obscured by draped fabric.

24
00:02:19.537 --> 00:02:24.831
An old woman was in front of one of the huts, stirring something in a brass pot.

25
00:02:24.832 --> 00:02:28.990
She stared at Zann and Gliss with dark, sunken eyes.

26
00:02:28.991 --> 00:02:34.915
"Beware, my young Red friends," she said, her voice coarse and deep.

27
00:02:34.916 --> 00:02:39.326
"There are trolls all over town looking for your kind."

28
00:02:39.327 --> 00:02:43.991
"Oh no!" Gliss squeaked. "What if they see us?"

29
00:02:43.992 --> 00:02:52.205
"I can help," the woman said. "I have scarves to cover your hair and a paste to hide your freckles."

30
00:02:52.206 --> 00:02:56.217
"Really?" Gliss sounded relieved. "Thank you!"

31
00:02:56.218 --> 00:03:00.546
"Not so fast." The woman held up a hand.

32
00:03:00.547 --> 00:03:05.633
"I am just a poor merchant and cannot afford to give away my wares.

33
00:03:05.634 --> 00:03:08.552
What do you have to offer me in trade?"

34
00:03:08.553 --> 00:03:17.163
"Trade?" Zann was confused. Since most people used magic for their daily needs, trading was uncommon except among Voids.

35
00:03:17.164 --> 00:03:20.180
"We have nothing of value," Darb said.

36
00:03:20.181 --> 00:03:23.482
"Perhaps we can pay you for the disguises later."

37
00:03:23.483 --> 00:03:30.248
"Nothing of value?" The woman had spotted Zing. "The fire whistler—is it yours?"

38
00:03:30.249 --> 00:03:35.011
"Yes," Zann said. "But he's not for trade at any price!"

39
00:03:35.012 --> 00:03:38.241
"A shame." Her eyes lingered on the dragon.

40
00:03:38.242 --> 00:03:40.890
"Then I'm afraid I cannot help you."

41
00:03:40.891 --> 00:03:46.703
"Please!" Perda stepped forward. "If you only knew why we've come here, you'd—"

42
00:03:46.704 --> 00:03:49.764
"Never mind," Zann interrupted quickly.

43
00:03:49.765 --> 00:03:55.722
Even though the woman had warned them about the trolls, there was something about her that Zann didn't quite trust.

44
00:03:55.723 --> 00:03:59.032
"We'll figure out another way to disguise ourselves."

45
00:03:59.033 --> 00:04:02.643
The old woman shrugged. "Good luck to you then."

46
00:04:02.644 --> 00:04:05.369
She turned her attention back to her pot.

47
00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:09.496
Darb and the girls were already moving on, but Zann hesitated.

48
00:04:09.497 --> 00:04:14.473
"So is it true?" he asked the woman. "About the wormhole, I mean.

49
00:04:14.474 --> 00:04:18.383
Is there really a passage to other worlds near this tree?"

50
00:04:18.384 --> 00:04:22.288
"I have no idea what you're talking about," she replied.

51
00:04:22.289 --> 00:04:27.733
"Though I could try to find out. For a price, of course."

52
00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:33.893
Zann frowned, suddenly certain that she knew much more about the wormhole than she was admitting.

53
00:04:33.894 --> 00:04:41.671
"I'd ask my parents," he blurted out angrily, "but they disappeared through a wormhole much like this one four years ago!"

54
00:04:41.672 --> 00:04:45.086
He bit his lip, wishing he hadn't said that out loud.

55
00:04:45.087 --> 00:04:53.149
Now the woman was studying his face curiously, a hint of recognition in her eyes. Or was that his imagination?

56
00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:55.035
"Wait here," she commanded.

57
00:04:55.036 --> 00:05:02.968
She disappeared into her hut. Soon she was back, pressing a wad of fabric and a small glass vial into Zann's hands.

58
00:05:02.969 --> 00:05:09.210
"Take these," she said. "It's my gift to you as . . . as a visitor to Wormwood."

59
00:05:09.211 --> 00:05:13.345
She handed the items to Zann and then went back to stirring her pot.

60
00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:16.979
"Zann?" Perda called. "What are you doing?"

61
00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:27.011
"That woman just gave me these." He hurried over to his friends and unfurled a couple of long, gauzy scarves while Gliss grabbed the vial and examined it.

62
00:05:27.012 --> 00:05:32.576
"It's the disguise stuff!" she exclaimed. "Why'd the woman change her mind?"

63
00:05:32.577 --> 00:05:36.093
"Who knows, but I'm glad she did," Perda said.

64
00:05:36.094 --> 00:05:38.656
"I'll help you with your scarf, Zann."

65
00:05:38.657 --> 00:05:43.874
While Perda fussed with Zann's hair, Gliss covered her freckles with the liquid from the vial.

66
00:05:43.875 --> 00:05:47.493
The whole time Zann couldn't help staring at the woman.

67
00:05:47.494 --> 00:05:52.705
What had it meant, that glimmer of recognition he'd seen after mentioning his parents?

68
00:05:52.706 --> 00:05:56.019
Could she possibly know something about what had happened to them?

69
00:05:56.020 --> 00:06:01.751
"There!" Perda finished Zann's disguise. "Now nobody will know you're a Red."

70
00:06:01.752 --> 00:06:04.012
"How do I look?" Gliss asked.

71
00:06:04.013 --> 00:06:09.832
Zann barely heard them. He wanted to walk over and demand to know what the woman knew.

72
00:06:09.833 --> 00:06:13.621
But no matter how much he wanted to do that, he knew he couldn't.

73
00:06:13.622 --> 00:06:20.041
Not right now. Boz, his friends, and possibly all of Magica were relying on him.

74
00:06:20.042 --> 00:06:28.217
"Let's get moving," he said. "It's still a long walk to the palace."
